de2e00ae (2766 1792808687332 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f324") (src . "landing-freeze: a structural draft behind an unrelated commit is moved onto the applied cut\n\nA freeze whose writer held a `new` or `delete` draft at an older cut was\nrefused `drafts-behind-conflict` naming it, even when the draft still applied\nunchanged at the applied cut; the detour was to discard the draft and lay it\nagain from the same bytes. Now:\n\n- `landing-freeze` judges each structural draft against the store as applied:\n  current at the applied cut; moved when a new file's path no live file holds\n  there, or a delete's file still has the draft's `based-on` as its baseline;\n  conflict otherwise (a new file's path held, a deleted file gone or changed),\n  which is still refused `drafts-behind-conflict` with nothing written.\n- The move is working.sc's `working-move-structural!`: the entry is rewritten\n  in place at the applied cut under one hold of the writer's draft lock, with\n  the same bytes, path and language and a version recomputed for the new cut,\n  and only while it is still the version the freeze judged (a draft written\n  again since is refused `structural-changed`). Nothing is removed first: a\n  refusal or a failure before the rename leaves the entry where it was; a\n  failure of the directory flush after the rename leaves the whole new entry\n  at the applied cut. Either way the freeze is refused\n  `(error structural-move-refused (key <k>) (answer ...))` and a second freeze\n  reads the entry as it stands. `--check` names such a draft under `moved` in\n  its `refreeze` answer and writes nothing.\n- `REBASED.sexp` records `(moved <key> (from-cut <cut>) (to-cut <cut>))` for a\n  structural draft, as it did `(moved <block> ...)` for a block.\n- Hold stages `freeze-before-move` and `structural-move-before-write`; fault\n  `fsync-fail@working:dir=structural` pins what the flush failure leaves.\n- Rows ST-M1..M7 in test/drafts-tools.sc (68); README `landing-freeze` section\n  and tools/landing-freeze.sc header say the same.\n- Two README gaps closed: the `query` counts paragraph reads 26 fact\n  relations, 21 rule relations and 43 rules (test/query-kinds.sc README-3 now\n  reads each number from the paragraph and compares it with the table it\n  cites); `uses`'s describe text says a Scheme text block is read as forms\n  first and falls back to tokens only when a part does not read.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 461))))
